Article 167

Special Protection for Children as referred to in Article 166 letter is provided to: Children in emergency situations; a.

Children in conflict with the law;

Children from minority and isolated groups; c.

Children who are exploited economically and/or sexually;

Children who are victims of narcotics, alcohol, psychotropic, and other addictive substance abuse and/or involved in their production/distribution;

Children who are victims of pornography; f.

Children with HIV/AIDS; g.

Children who are victims of abduction, sale and/or trafficking in persons;

Children who are victims of physical and/or psychological violence;

Hp

Children who are victims of sexual crimes;

k. Children who are victims of terrorist networks;

Children with Disabilities;

Children who are victims of abuse and neglect;

Children with deviant social behavior; and

Children who are victims of stigmatization from labeling related to the condition of their Parents.

Article 23

In order to implement the objective of providing protection for Women's rights from various forms of violence and other discriminatory treatment as referred to in Article 20 letter, is carried out through: a. promotive efforts;

b. preventive efforts;

c. curative efforts; and

d. rehabilitative efforts, in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations.

Article 53

Integrated services for Women victims of violence as referred to in Article 52 shall be implemented by adhering to principles, which include:

a. gender responsive; non-discriminatory; equal and respectful relationships; maintaining confidentiality; providing a sense of security and comfort;

Ho respecting individual differences; f. non-judgmental; respecting the choices and decisions of victims; sensitive to the background and condition of victims and i. use of language that is appropriate and understood by victims; fast and simple;

k. empathy; and fulfillment of Women's rights.

