CHAPTER II

OBLIGATIONS AND RESPONSIBILITIES

REGIONAL GOVERNMENT

Article

The Regional Government is responsible for guaranteeing and making maximum efforts to respect Women and Children in accordance with their dignity without distinguishing ethnicity, religion, race, class, gender, ethnicity, culture and language, legal status, and physical and mental condition.

-1ll1- Article

The Regional Government has the obligation and responsibility in organizing the protection of Women and Children in the Region.

Article

The obligation and responsibility for organizing the Protection of Women and Children as referred to in Article 7, is carried out by the Agency.

Article

The organization of protection for Women and Children in addition to being carried out by the Agency, is also the obligation and responsibility of related Regional Apparatuses handling Governmental affairs, as follows:

Education;

Health;

Social Affairs;

Population and Civil Registration;

Population Control and Family Planning; Manpower;

